                    alloc_champions:        `Clinical champions / opinion leaders — and a plan to sustain them past the pilot`,
                    alloc_epr:              `EPR integration & forcing-functions — the tool embedded in the electronic record`,
                    alloc_audit:            `Audit-and-feedback dashboards — ward-level use and outcome data fed back to teams`,
                    alloc_education:        `Education & simulation training for the inconsistent and workaround users`,
                    alloc_passive:          `Passive dissemination — trust-wide email, an intranet guideline and a launch webinar`,
                    forcing_balanced:       `Balanced — embed it as the EPR default but keep clinical override and pair it with champions and feedback`,
                    forcing_mandatory:      `Hard-wire mandatory, non-overridable alerts — make non-use impossible`,
                    forcing_persuasion:     `Persuasion only — leave it opt-in and rely on champions and education to win hearts`,

                    r3_case_label:          `Build the board case — how do you justify the £1.8M + £420K/yr against a £12M deficit?`,
                    r3_route_label:         `Choose the funding route under the deficit.`,
                    r3_value_label:         `Quantify the reputational and regulatory (CQC) value of sustained adoption?`,
                    r3_sensitivity_label:   `Stress-test the case: at what adoption rate does the investment still hold? Set your committed floor (%).`,
                    r3_sensitivity_readout: `Adoption floor the case is stress-tested to:`,
                    r3_pct:                 `%`,
                    r3_sensitivity_hint:    `The finance director will ask what happens at 40% adoption. A case that only works at 75% is not a fundable case.`,
                    case_costavoid:         `Translate the clinical benefit into freed bed-days, avoided litigation and the mortality benefit — a costed cost-avoidance case`,
                    case_clinical:          `Lead on the clinical benefit alone — it saves lives and cuts length-of-stay; that should be enough`,
                    case_mandate:           `Argue it is a safety mandate the board cannot refuse, and leave the numbers vague`,
                    route_investtosave:     `Invest-to-save / phased — fund from the freed bed-days it generates, staged against adoption milestones`,
                    route_central:          `Demand central capital up front — the full £1.8M now, deficit or not`,
                    route_defer:            `Defer — wait for next year's budget when the deficit might ease`,
                    value_quantify:         `Yes — put a credible figure on CQC rating risk and reputational value, alongside the bed-days`,
                    value_mention:          `Mention it qualitatively — note it matters but do not size it`,
                    value_skip:             `Skip it — the board only cares about hard cash`,

                    r4_owner_label:         `Design the routinization mechanism — who owns the pathway after the project team disbands?`,
                    r4_checkpoint_label:    `It is the 9-month checkpoint — adoption sits near the 60% gate. How do you present it?`,
                    r4_consultant_label:    `A senior consultant publicly disputes the algorithm's false-positive rate and threatens to opt his department out. Your move?`,
                    r4_resolve_label:       `How firmly do you resolve to keep the structural lever AND the clinical credibility, not trade one for the other? (%)`,
                    owner_governance:       `A named clinical owner backed by a sepsis governance group, standing audit, EPR default and induction — ownership survives any one person`,
                    owner_champion:         `Dr. Ahmed, the brilliant pilot champion — keep the whole thing resting on the hero who built it`,
                    owner_project:          `The project team, extended for another year, then we will work out handover later`,
                    check_path75:           `Show the evidence AND the concrete mechanisms keeping the curve climbing to 75% by 24 months — go-live is not the finish line`,
                    check_celebrate:        `Declare victory — we cleared the gate, celebrate the win and ease off the effort`,
                    check_defend:           `Defend the number defensively and hope it holds on its own`,
                    consult_engage:         `Treat the resistance as data — tune the algorithm with him on the review group, address alert fatigue, and keep the EPR default`,
                    consult_overrule:       `Overrule him — hard-wire the alerts harder and frame him as obstruction to be managed around`,
                    consult_concede:        `Concede — drop the forcing-function and let departments opt out to keep the peace`,

                    warn_diag_range:        `Diagnostic rigour must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
                    warn_alloc_negative:    `Rollout-envelope allocations cannot be negative.`,
                    warn_alloc_total:       `The rollout envelope must total exactly £1.80M — that is the capital you secured. Re-balance.`,
                    warn_sensitivity_range: `The adoption floor must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
